course: dictionary
lesson: 9342
title: A word for pointed towers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spire is a tall, thin, pointed shape that rises to a point at the top, a bit like a cone. You will most often see one on top of a church tower, reaching up towards the sky.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years, until its spire fell in 1548.» The sentence says the building was tallest until its spire fell, so the spire must be the pointed top part of the building. Try it: "until its pointed top fell" still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe things in nature. A rock spire is a tall, pointed rock, and the tip of a tree can be a spire too. So spire is not only a church word: any tall, thin, pointed shape can be one.
fact: A spire is a tall, pointed, cone-shaped structure on top of a building, usually on a church tower.
fact: «The city of dreaming spires» is a nickname for Oxford, because it has many tall, pointed church towers.
fact: Salisbury Cathedral has the tallest church spire in the UK.
fact: A spire is often shaped like a cone or a pyramid.
fact: A spire can also be a tall, thin, pointed rock or the tip of a tree.
exercise: «The spire of the church could be seen from miles away.» What is a spire? | A wide, flat field | *A tall, pointed structure on top of a building | A deep hole in the ground | A small, round window
exercise: Oxford is called «the city of dreaming spires». What are the spires in this name? | Trees in the park | *Tall, pointed tops of buildings | Boats on the water | Wide shops along the river
exercise: Which of these can also be called a spire? | A soft, round cushion | *A tall, thin, pointed rock | A wide, flat lake | A long, slow river
test: «Salisbury Cathedral has the tallest church spire in the UK.» What does spire mean in this sentence? | The path to the door | The bell inside the church | The graves in the churchyard | *The tall, pointed top of the church tower
test: A spire is often shaped like which solid? | A cube | A flat sheet | *A cone | A ball
exam: In «until its spire fell in 1548», what does spire mean? | *The tall, pointed top of the building | A stone wall around the city | A bell that rang each hour | A window of coloured glass
